body:
#### PR description:

This PR fixes three bugs in the seeds that `LSTOutputConverter` makes for mkFit (HLT default menu; offline `highPtTripletStep` in the LST workflows).

- **pT3/pT5 hit order.** A pixel-track OT hit and an LST hit on overlapping modules of one layer were sorted by the module's `rSpan().first` (`|zSpan().first|` in the endcap), which can tie or invert in the tilted barrel. `makeSeed` then failed for 8-9% of the pT3/pT5 objects in the HLT, and their seeds fell back to the pixel seed without LST's OT hits. Hits are now sorted by layer, then by the distance of the sensor plane from the origin along the plane normal (the plane's radius in the flat barrel, its |z| in the endcap).
- **T4 helix start.** It could use the two hits of one module. Then 1.5-3% of the T4 objects gave no seed, and another 15-17% got a seed with a badly measured curvature, part of them below the 0.8 GeV LST cut (plots below). T5 and T4 now share one rule: the helix starts from two hits on different modules, neither on a PS strip sensor.
- **Empty seed.** A failed inner-tracker-only pLS seed read `seeds[0]` from an empty vector; the input pixel seed is now kept.

Duplicate rate of the LST seeds for mkFit in the HLT (ttbar, QCD). The seeds below 0.5 GeV go from about one per event on master to 0.01-0.02.

<img src="https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/desc/seed_duplrate_pt_ttbar.png" width="350"> <img src="https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/desc/seed_duplrate_pt_qcd.png" width="350">

#### PR validation:

CMSSW_20_1_X_2026-11-09-1100 with only this PR. Master  this PR, CPU, PU200, the same events (ttbar / QCD):
- HLT, 5000 + 5000 events, hltGeneralTracks:
  - prompt efficiency (vxy < 2.5 cm): 89.20%  89.20% / 88.86%  88.87%, unchanged;
  - efficiency at vxy 32-60 cm: 51.2%  53.3% / 41.6%  43.4%;
  - fake rate: 1.07%  1.05% / 1.27%  1.24%;
  - duplicate rate: 1.00%  1.01% / 0.98%  1.00%;
  - +0.10 hits per track.

  Plots: [ttbar](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/hlt_ttbar/plots_hlt.html), [QCD](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/hlt_qcd/plots_hlt.html)
- Offline 34634.711, 2000 + 2000 events, generalTracks (only the T4 fix acts offline: offline pixel seeds have no OT hits):
  - efficiency: 88.66%  88.67% / 86.36%  86.34%;
  - efficiency at 32-63 cm production radius: 39.6%  40.1% / 29.8%  30.8%;
  - fake rate: 7.63%  7.60% / 7.68%  7.65%;
  - duplicate rate: 0.90%  0.91% / 0.90%  0.91%.

  Plots: [ttbar](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/off01_ttbar/index.html), [QCD](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/off01_qcd/index.html); all iterations (34634.714), 500 + 500 events: [ttbar](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/offall_ttbar/index.html), [QCD](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/offall_qcd/index.html)
- HLT timing, CPU menu, ttbar, thread time per event (8 jobs  16 threads): converter 55.1  44.9 ms, mkFit 62.7  57.6 ms, whole job 0.9%.
